[
  {
    "step_title": "Service account",
    "items": [
      {
        "desc": "Synology MCP lets Claude (claude.ai, Claude Code) manage this NAS. It acts on DSM with a dedicated account in the <b>administrators</b> group: create it first in Control Panel → User & Group if needed. What Claude may do is then set part by part in the app."
      },
      {
        "type": "combobox",
        "desc": "DSM account the server acts with:",
        "subitems": [
          {
            "key": "wizard_username",
            "desc": "Account",
            "displayField": "name",
            "valueField": "name",
            "editable": true,
            "mode": "remote",
            "api_store": {
              "api": "SYNO.Core.User",
              "method": "list",
              "version": 1,
              "baseParams": {
                "offset": 0,
                "limit": -1
              },
              "root": "users",
              "idProperty": "name",
              "fields": [
                "name"
              ]
            },
            "validator": {
              "allowBlank": false
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "password",
        "subitems": [
          {
            "key": "wizard_password",
            "desc": "Password",
            "validator": {
              "allowBlank": false
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "desc": "If this account uses 2-step verification, the app will ask for a code after the installation."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "step_title": "Next steps",
    "items": [
      {
        "desc": "After the installation, open <b>Synology MCP</b> from the DSM main menu to:<br>• set up Internet access (reverse proxy rule and certificate configured automatically);<br>• choose the rights of each part (off, read-only, read-write) and the allowed accounts;<br>• get the address to give Claude, follow the sessions and the action log."
      }
    ]
  }
]
